  "body": "Expose external NC file simulation through the MCP server (`crates/app/src/mcp/`) and `camcraft-cli` (`crates/app/src/cli.rs`).\n\n## Scope\n- Add `simulate_gcode` in `crates/app/src/mcp/` accepting `path`, optional `dialect`, optional `tools` map (`T -> tool name`), and optional setup overrides.\n- Call the NC simulation runner from #2218 (`crates/app`) and return JSON with section counts, deviation summary, missing `T` numbers, and line-numbered findings.\n- Refuse unmapped tools, missing stock, or parse errors with `isError: true` and the line number.\n- Support rendering the simulated NC stock through `render_stock` (`crates/app/src/mcp/render.rs`) or an inline summary.\n- Add the matching verb in `crates/app/src/script/api.rs` and `camcraft-cli` usage (`crates/app/src/cli.rs`).\n\nDepends on #2218.\n\nDone means: An MCP integration test runs `simulate_gcode` on an `.nc` fixture with tool bindings, returns JSON findings with 1-based line numbers, renders the simulated stock, and refuses unmapped tools with `isError: true`.\n\nPart of #2213\n",
